{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BjEuY6XJgBHySwLK6gn1Dr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the research context carefully to define three tiers for the Dream simulation.\n\nKey facts from the project:\n- SICA = Symbolic Invariant Consensus Aggregation - uses MAX-SAT over extracted constraints to resolve Self-Consistency ties\n- Core metric: C0 (multi-candidate rate) determines when SICA helps\n- Existing data from sica_d012_14b (60 questions): SICA 73.3% vs SC 70.0%, gap +3.3pp, C0=53.3%, bootstrap p=0.2261\n- FOLIO subset: SICA 80% vs SC 73.3% (+6.7pp)\n\n\n- ProofWriter subset shows no improvement (SICA and SC both 66.7%), while QwQ-32B's low C0 of 3.6% confirms the operating regime claim where SICA equals SC\n- Currently running exp-001 with 804 questions for expanded evaluation, with pending experiments across different model families and constraint ablations to test K sensitivity\n- The paper's three core claims center on principled tiebreaking, characterizing when C0 governs effectiveness, and establishing C0 as a practical diagnostic tool\n\nNow I'm defining the three tiers based on what could happen with the expanded experiments: best case shows strong, statistically significant gains with cross-family validation and clear evidence that MaxSAT constraints matter; median case shows smaller gains with marginal significance and mixed cross-family results; worst case shows SICA performing no better than SC overall, which would require pivoting to an analysis paper instead. I need to track the SICA-SC gap, p-values, C0 values across models, cross-family consistency, and the differential impact of MaxSAT versus count-only constraints. Looking at the baseline data from D012, I had a +3.3pp gap with p=0.2261 and C0=53.3%, while FOLIO alone showed +6.7pp.\n\nNow scaling to 804 questions where ProofWriter dominates at 75% of the dataset but showed 0pp gain on the smaller sample, while FOLIO showed +6.7pp. In the best scenario, FOLIO maintains its gains around +5-8pp and ProofWriter picks up some improvement too, creating a combined significant effect. The median case has FOLIO holding at +3-5pp but ProofWriter staying flat, resulting in a small combined gap that's only marginally significant. Worst case is FOLIO's gains shrinking as the dataset grows and ProofWriter remaining at 0 or negative, leaving the combined effect at or below +1pp with no statistical significance.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12568,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12568},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36a6fd08-a2ec-491f-8113-e6325a459153","uuid":"46980841-a9dd-4823-ad31-0656e5374b12"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BjEuY6XJgBHySwLK6gn1Dr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"exp-001 confirms gains with statistical significance; cross-family and ablation all validate\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - FOLIO gain sustains at +4pp or above on 204 questions\n      - ProofWriter shows modest positive gap (+1-3pp) on 600 questions\n      - Combined gap statistically significant (p<0.05 bootstrap)\n      - Cross-family (Mistral/LLaMA) both show C0>25% and positive SICA-SC gap\n      - Constraint ablation shows MaxSAT > count-only by ≥2pp\n      - C0 shows gradient across model scales (7B>14B>72B)\n    number_ranges:\n      combined_gap_pp: [2.5, 5.0]\n      folio_gap_pp: [4.0, 8.0]\n      proofwriter_gap_pp: [1.0, 3.0]\n      bootstrap_p_combined: [0.01, 0.05]\n      c0_14b_expanded: [0.35, 0.55]\n      c0_mistral_7b: [0.30, 0.60]\n      c0_llama_8b: [0.30, 0.60]\n      cross_family_gap_pp: [1.5, 5.0]\n      maxsat_vs_count_only_pp: [2.0, 5.0]\n      tiebreak_win_rate: [0.70, 0.85]\n    narrative_direction: \"Original framing holds — SICA is a principled, effective method with formally characterizable operating regime. All 3 claims stand at full strength. Hero figure (C0 vs gap scatter) shows clean threshold with gradient. Paper tells a complete story: method + when it works + why + how to know in advance.\"\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"FOLIO gain holds but PW dilutes; combined significance marginal; cross-family partially validates\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - FOLIO sustains +3-5pp on 204 questions (positive but smaller than D012's +6.7)\n      - ProofWriter shows ~0pp on 600 questions (no gain, no loss)\n      - Combined gap exists (+1-2pp) but p≈0.05-0.15 (marginal)\n      - At least 2/3 cross-family models show expected C0 pattern\n      - One cross-family model shows anomalous C0 or negative gap\n      - Constraint ablation shows MaxSAT ≥ count-only but difference small (<2pp)\n      - C0 gradient exists but noisy (7B>>14B, 72B not clearly lower than 14B)\n    number_ranges:\n      combined_gap_pp: [1.0, 2.5]\n      folio_gap_pp: [3.0, 5.0]\n      proofwriter_gap_pp: [-0.5, 1.0]\n      bootstrap_p_combined: [0.05, 0.15]\n      c0_14b_expanded: [0.30, 0.50]\n      c0_mistral_7b: [0.20, 0.45]\n      c0_llama_8b: [0.20, 0.45]\n      cross_family_gap_pp: [0.0, 3.0]\n      maxsat_vs_count_only_pp: [0.5, 2.0]\n      tiebreak_win_rate: [0.60, 0.75]\n    narrative_direction: \"Claim 1 weakened: reframe as 'principled tiebreaking with interpretability advantage' rather than 'accuracy improvement'. Claim 2 (operating regime) becomes primary contribution — C0 characterization is robust even if absolute gains are modest. Claim 3 holds as binary indicator (C0 high/low) rather than continuous predictor. Paper pivots emphasis to 'When does symbolic consensus help?' analysis framing. FOLIO presented as domain where formal structure aligns with method; PW as partial-structure domain. Need exp-013 ablation to defend MaxSAT over simpler alternatives, or concede to 'weighted counting suffices'. Still targets EMNLP Main but accepts Findings as realistic outcome.\"\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"Expanded results show SICA ≈ SC; gains vanish with scale; pivot to analysis/characterization paper\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - FOLIO gap shrinks to ≤+2pp on 204 questions (D012's +6.7 was small-sample artifact)\n      - ProofWriter shows 0 or slightly negative gap\n      - Combined gap ≤+1pp, not significant (p>0.2)\n      - C0 pattern still holds (high C0 for instruction models, low for reasoning models)\n      - But high C0 does NOT translate to SICA>SC — diversity exists but MaxSAT doesn't exploit it effectively\n      - Constraint extraction quality is the bottleneck (noisy FOL, wrong exclusions)\n      - Cross-family shows similar pattern — C0 high but gap ≈ 0\n    number_ranges:\n      combined_gap_pp: [-0.5, 1.0]\n      folio_gap_pp: [0.0, 2.5]\n      proofwriter_gap_pp: [-1.5, 0.5]\n      bootstrap_p_combined: [0.15, 0.50]\n      c0_14b_expanded: [0.30, 0.55]\n      c0_mistral_7b: [0.20, 0.50]\n      c0_llama_8b: [0.20, 0.50]\n      cross_family_gap_pp: [-1.0, 1.5]\n      maxsat_vs_count_only_pp: [-1.0, 1.0]\n      tiebreak_win_rate: [0.50, 0.65]\n    narrative_direction: \"Activate D023 contingency. Core reframe: 'Characterizing When Symbolic Consensus Methods Fail — and Why Trace Diversity Is Necessary But Not Sufficient.' Claim 1 becomes 'SICA provides interpretable tiebreaking' (no accuracy claim). Claim 2 survives intact — operating regime characterization is the paper's primary contribution, now framed as explaining failure modes. New angle: C0 measures output diversity but constraint extraction quality is the missing second condition. Add constraint-quality-vs-gap correlation analysis (CPU-only). Claim 3 reframes as 'C0 as necessary condition diagnostic' (high C0 needed but not sufficient). The intellectual contribution is the negative-result insight: why naive symbolic aggregation doesn't straightforwardly improve over voting despite intuitive appeal. Target EMNLP Findings (primary) or AAAI 2027 Main (fallback with additional method improvements).\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12568,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12568},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36a6fd08-a2ec-491f-8113-e6325a459153","uuid":"511628c8-989e-4a57-b791-1c19a6b7440f"}
